
Atop a large green hill

This hill is larger than the ones around it, though
it looks much the same otherwise. Beneath your feet
is some of the springiest grass you've ever set 
foot upon. It rustles in the slightest breeze, making
shimmering green waves as far as you can see. This hill,
you realize, affords a commanding view of the surrounding
countryside as you pause to look around. To the
west and southwest, the seemingly endless hills get gradually
smaller and give way to rippling plains. You breathe in
deeply and notice the faint stench of stagnent water in
the air that indicates that swampland must be fairly close by.


